  "note": "The room is in audition: Two writers write the same opening pages at the same time, blind to each other. You pick the voice.\n\nThis is the audition. Write pages 1-3 only, in full, into your audition file. The other writer is writing the same pages and you cannot see their work.\n\nDrawability: Pages are drawn by an image model, one page per generation, from each character's and location's sheet, and a page drifts when it carries too much. So: at most 4 panels a page; at most 3 named characters in one panel; one location a page where the story allows (every new location needs its own sheet); no crowd that must be recognisable; a big moment gets a splash (one panel, the whole page). Count pages this way, not by comic convention. Every page you make keeps to it.\n\nThe book is exactly 4 pages: pages 1-4, no more, no fewer.",
